{"ghsa_id":"GHSA-r53p-7pc4-xj5r","cve_id":"CVE-2026-18540","url":"https://api.github.com/advisories/GHSA-r53p-7pc4-xj5r","html_url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-r53p-7pc4-xj5r","summary":"undici vulnerable to downstream response splitting via retry interceptor","description":"### Impact\n\nUndici's `interceptors.retry()` can resume a request after a partial response and append the resumed bytes to an already partially delivered body, while the application still receives the original response's status and headers. When that response carried a `Content-Length`, the application can receive a longer body. Applications that forward Undici's status, headers, and body downstream without recalculating framing, for example proxy or gateway applications, may emit a response whose body exceeds the forwarded `Content-Length`, and the excess bytes can be read as the start of a subsequent HTTP response (downstream response splitting or desynchronization).\n\nFor example, a `404 Not Found` with `Content-Length: 2` that sends one byte then closes can be resumed with an open-ended `Range` request, and the resumed `206 Partial Content` bytes are appended, so the application receives more than two body bytes while still seeing `Content-Length: 2`. The bug requires `interceptors.retry()` enabled, an attacker-controlled or faulty upstream, and a downstream forwarder that does not recalculate `Content-Length`.\n\n### Patches\n\nPatched in undici v6.28.1, v7.29.1, and v8.10.2. Upgrade to one of these or later.\n\n### Workarounds\n\n- Disable `interceptors.retry()` for untrusted upstreams, or set `maxRetries: 0`.\n- Remove or recalculate `Content-Length` before forwarding a response body assembled by Undici.","type":"reviewed","severity":"low","repository_advisory_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nodejs/undici/security-advisories/GHSA-r53p-7pc4-xj5r","source_code_location":"https://github.com/nodejs/undici","identifiers":[{"value":"GHSA-r53p-7pc4-xj5r","type":"GHSA"},{"value":"CVE-2026-18540","type":"CVE"}],"references":["https://github.com/nodejs/undici/security/advisories/GHSA-r53p-7pc4-xj5r","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-18540","https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/0160a719063fb0a77f4fdf9500b9166b91e14329","https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/cd8af90b38ae33c2838d54a2d629774122effe95","https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/ce31bc824b578008faae5d3350da66c1b5f71548","https://hackerone.com/reports/3900104","https://hackerone.com/reports/3900615","https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html","https://github.com/nodejs/undici/releases/tag/v6.28.1","https://github.com/nodejs/undici/releases/tag/v7.29.1","https://github.com/nodejs/undici/releases/tag/v8.10.2","https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-r53p-7pc4-xj5r"],"published_at":"2026-09-29T18:22:07Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T18:22:08Z","github_reviewed_at":"2026-09-29T18:22:07Z","nvd_published_at":"2026-09-04T18:17:50Z","withdrawn_at":null,"vulnerabilities":[{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"undici"},"vulnerable_version_range":"< 6.28.1","first_patched_version":"6.28.1","vulnerable_functions":[]},{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"undici"},"vulnerable_version_range":">= 7.0.0, < 7.29.1","first_patched_version":"7.29.1","vulnerable_functions":[]},{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"undici"},"vulnerable_version_range":">= 8.0.0, < 8.10.2","first_patched_version":"8.10.2","vulnerable_functions":[]}],"cvss_severities":{"cvss_v3":{"vector_string":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:N","score":3.7},"cvss_v4":{"vector_string":null,"score":0.0}},"cwes":[{"cwe_id":"CWE-444","name":"Inconsistent Interpretation of HTTP Requests ('HTTP Request/Response Smuggling')"}],"credits":[{"user":{"login":"samuel871211","id":55658154,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NjU4MTU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55658154?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuel871211","html_url":"https://github.com/samuel871211","followers_url":"https://api.github